# Strix AI Penetration Testing (Cursor Rule)

Use the **Strix** skill (`skills/strix/SKILL.md`, `.agents/skills/strix/SKILL.md`) when the user wants to penetration test, vulnerability-scan, or find-and-fix weaknesses in applications, websites, or services they own or are explicitly authorized to test.

## Core behavior
- Strix is an open-source AI penetration testing agent (usestrix/strix) that runs autonomous AI hackers against targets and proposes remediation.
- Only targets the user owns or has explicit, written authorization to test. Unauthorized testing is prohibited and illegal in most jurisdictions.
- Strix output (cloud scans, `strix cloud vulns list --severity critical --json`) can be fed back into REA skills for reverse-engineering and remediation of affected components.

## Suggested workflow
1. Confirm target ownership/authorization before proceeding.
2. Run Strix scan (local or `strix cloud scans start ... --wait`).
3. Review vulnerabilities (`strix cloud vulns list --severity critical`).
4. Route findings to REA skills (e.g., `website-security-audit`, binary disassembly, source recovery) for root-cause analysis and fixes.